+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-18-harden-apply-patch-validation/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+## Why
+
+Users of `applyPatch` report patches being accepted that they consider invalid. A review found that validation lets some non-conforming patches through: a sparse array patch (holes are skipped by `Array.prototype.map`), an operation whose `value` is present but `undefined` (not a JSON value), and operation members (`op`, `path`, `from`) that are read through the prototype chain rather than being own members of the operation object.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Reject a patch array with holes (RFC 6902 §3: every element must be an operation object).
+- Reject `add`, `replace` and `test` operations whose `value` is `undefined` (RFC 8259: not a JSON value).
+- Read `op`, `path` and `from` only as own members of the operation object.
+- Not breaking for valid patches (JSON-parsed patches are unaffected); only previously accepted malformed input now throws `JsonPatchError`.
+
+Governing standard: RFC 6902 §3–§5, RFC 6901 §3–§4, RFC 8259 for JSON values.
+
+Out of scope: root removal (kept as an error, documented in the spec), JSON Merge Patch, in-place patching.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: stricter patch and operation validation.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts` (`applyPatch`, `parseOperation`); `test/json-patch.test.ts`.
+- No dependencies added.
