@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+## MODIFIED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Patch shape and validation
+Per RFC 6902 §3, a patch SHALL be an array of operation objects. Every index of the array SHALL hold an operation object; a sparse array (with holes) SHALL be an error. Each operation SHALL have an own string `op` member that is one of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`, and an own string `path` that is a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3). `add`, `replace` and `test` SHALL have an own `value` member that is a JSON value (RFC 8259), including `null` but not `undefined`; `move` and `copy` SHALL have an own string `from` that is a valid JSON Pointer. Members inherited through the prototype chain SHALL NOT count. Members not defined for the operation SHALL be ignored. Any violation SHALL cause an error to be thrown. An empty patch SHALL return a document equal to the input.
+
+#### Scenario: Patch is not an array
+- **WHEN** the patch is an object, `null`, a string or `undefined`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Patch has holes
+- **WHEN** the patch is a sparse array such as `[ <empty> ]` or `[{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":1}, <empty>]`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Operation is not an object
+- **WHEN** an element of the patch is `null`, an array or a primitive
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or unknown op
+- **WHEN** an operation has no `op`, a non-string `op`, or an `op` such as `"merge"` or `"ADD"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid path
+- **WHEN** an operation has no `path`, a non-string `path`, or a path that is not a valid pointer such as `"a"` or `"/a~2"`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Missing value
+- **WHEN** an `add`, `replace` or `test` operation has no `value` member
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Undefined value
+- **WHEN** an `add`, `replace` or `test` operation has a `value` member that is `undefined`
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Null value is a value
+- **WHEN** `{"op":"add","path":"/a","value":null}` is applied to `{}`
+- **THEN** the result is `{"a":null}`
+
+#### Scenario: Missing or invalid from
+- **WHEN** a `move` or `copy` operation has no `from`, a non-string `from`, or an invalid pointer
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Inherited members do not count
+- **WHEN** `op`, `path` or `from` is only inherited from the operation's prototype
+- **THEN** an error is thrown
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown extra members
+- **WHEN** an operation has an additional member such as `"comment"`
+- **THEN** it is ignored
+
+#### Scenario: Empty patch
+- **WHEN** the patch is `[]`
+- **THEN** a document equal to the input is returned
